35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,A full pass takes over an hour and a half. That's a significant chunk of time when it all lands at once.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,I found out that some of us are barely here! And the kitchen use is totally uneven. It's not fair to split it equally.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It seems we have very different definitions of ""clean."" That's exactly where the resentment builds—when one person feels the other is lazy.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,It's a mess! We're buying the same spray twice and some people are paying for everything while others pay nothing!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The grout... it gets dirty again in eleven days. And the chat shows we only fight when we have to remind each other.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, while usage varies, the dirt still accumulates. The time cost is the real issue. Outsourcing might be the only logical way.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, but why should someone who is gone for a month pay the same as someone who lives here? We need a usage-based fee!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, the fact that we only fight when reminding each other suggests that ""reminding"" is the trigger. We need a system that removes the need to nag.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mio, I agree! But we need a clear monthly cost. No more ""paying back later."" We need a fixed pot of money!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,If it gets dirty so fast... maybe a schedule isn't enough. I just want to know it's clean without having to ask.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"The outside firm requires us to tidy up before they arrive. So we don't actually remove all the work, just the scrubbing.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"If we use a firm, we can split the cost based on how often we are actually in the house. That would be fair!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"I'm worried that a strict usage-based system will just lead to more tracking and more arguments about who used the kitchen for ""too long.""","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't care how we split it, as long as it's a fixed monthly amount and the receipts are public!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think a professional firm would be better. It would be the same standard every time. No more guessing.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
