60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is the most rational. It removes the time burden and ensures a professional standard, even if we still have to tidy.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I like C too, but only if we agree to split the cost based on presence. I can't support a flat split when some are gone for weeks!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I'm concerned about C's cost, but B is a recipe for disaster. The ""reminding"" and ""nagging"" in a rota will destroy our friendship.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option C is the best! We can just set a monthly budget for the cleaner and the supplies. No more ""who paid for the sponges?""","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I really prefer C. It's the only way I know the bathroom will actually be clean. I can't handle the unpredictability.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, we can settle the cost details after we choose the method. The priority is removing the labor hours from our schedules.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"If we can agree on a fair split, I'm in. I just don't want to go back to a system where the ""ghosts"" of the house get a free ride.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, @Mio, if we go with C, we must ensure the payment process is seamless. If we fight over the invoice, we've just traded one problem for another.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,That's why we need a shared fund! Everyone puts in their share at the start of the month. It's simple and fair!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I agree with @Rin. A shared fund would make it... easier. I wouldn't have to worry about the money or the cleaning.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A is too risky; some areas are harder than others, and it would lead to perceived unfairness. C is the only stable choice.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm convinced. As long as we acknowledge that usage and presence matter for the cost, C is the most balanced way forward.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. While it's an expense, the cost of a professional is lower than the cost of us not speaking to each other for a year.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! Let's do C! I'll help keep track of the money so nobody gets cheated. I'm very good at counting!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel much better about this. I can finally stop worrying about what I'll find when I open the door.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
